{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>But that the people are mighty, etc.</b> The meaning is: since in Moses' commission he asked ״Is it strong… are they in camps?״ etc., therefore they said that the people are mighty and dwell in fortresses, and they concluded by saying <b>and also the children of the Anak, etc.</b> — meaning, not to suppose that they fortified their cities because of their weakness; behold, we also saw the children of the Anak there, and these certainly have no fear — if so, one should not infer from their fortifications that they are weak." "<b>Further,</b> it intends by saying <b>the people that dwell in the land</b>, that the people were dwelling scattered outside the cities, relying on their might. And so you will find that they, of blessed memory, said (Numbers Rabbah 16:13) regarding the verse ״Amalek dwells… and the Canaanite,״ etc., that they were dwelling on the road outside the city. They also alluded, in the phrase <b>that dwell in the land</b>, that the land requires mighty warriors to stand in it."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:08:33.379702665Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}